@jennifer-shehane The latest version (`6.8.0`) behaves as described above, except for the upper-casing, which has thankfully been removed. AFAICS there's still no way to create custom commands that would create log entries looking just the same as native Cypress commands. That's because:

1. `Cypress.log` can produce custom log messages, but does so synchronously. Forcing the message into the command _execution_ flow with e.g. `wrap()` causes unwanted "nesting" of the output.
