@flotwig Yep, prior to 7.0 we were still using `cy.route` to override our apis since it wasn't possible to use `cy.intercept` in the same way. Since 7.0 dropped, we are trying to update everything to `cy.intercept` but noticed this bug along the way.

Overriding an alias using `cy.route` works in both 6.6 and 7.0:

```js
cy.server();
cy.intercept('/some/api', 'foo').as('someApi');
cy.route('/some/api', 'bar').as('someApi');
cy.window().then(win => {
  const req = new win.XMLHttpRequest();
  req.open('GET', '/some/api');
  req.send()
});
cy.wait('@someApi').then(interception => {
  // resolves with 'bar'
  console.log(interception.response.body);
});
```

In 7.0, switching the `cy.route` to `cy.intercept` results in the `cy.wait()` never resolving:

```js
cy.intercept('/some/api', 'foo').as('someApi');
cy.intercept('/some/api', 'bar').as('someApi');
cy.window().then(win => {
  const req = new win.XMLHttpRequest();
  req.open('GET', '/some/api');
