Hi!

The problem is the `htmlWebpackPluginBeforeHtmlProcessing` is deprecated in `html-webpack-plugin@4.x`. The lates version is 5.x - we support 4.x and 5.x as it stands. Vue CLI is still using `html-webpack-plugin@3.x`, and depends on those lifecycle hooks.

The first thing you could try is updating the Vue CLI and dependencies to the latest version. [Migrating from v3](https://cli.vuejs.org/migrating-from-v3/) and [migrating from v4](https://next.cli.vuejs.org/migrations/migrate-from-v4.html#upgrade-all-plugins-at-once). That should get you a more recent version of the `html-webpack-plugin` and PWA plugin.

______


We are exploring a solution to let us support any version of `html-webpack-plugin`. Until then, the easiest way to get your project to work, without upgrading your dependencies, would just be to conditionally remove the plugin when used with Cypress. [Here's an example of how to do that](https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/pull/15970). Example `cypress/plugins/index.js` file. The trick is you remove the plugin during testing, since you probably won't use a service working during development anyway.

```js
/// <reference types="cypress" />
const { startDevServer } = require('@cypress/webpack-dev-server')
const webpackConfig = require('@vue/cli-service/webpack.config')

/**
 * @type Cypress.PluginConfig
 */
module.exports = (on, config) => {
  on('dev-server:start', (options) => {

    // omit PWA Plugin during testing

    const modifiedWebpackConfig = {
      ...webpackConfig,
      plugins: (webpackConfig.plugins || []).filter((x) => {
        return x.constructor.name !== 'HtmlPwaPlugin'
      }),
    }

    return startDevServer({
      options,
      webpackConfig: modifiedWebpackConfig,
    })
  })

  return config
}
```

We should leave this issue open until we have a fix in Cypress.

