I faced the same issue with the **cypress-plugin-snapshots** plugin, for now I got it working with the following workaround.

Create your own **initPlugin** function without the event registration. I know this is not possible for every plugin but for **cypress-plugin-snapshots** it works.


```js
const { initConfig, CONFIG_KEY } = require('cypress-plugin-snapshots/src/config');
const initServer = require('cypress-plugin-snapshots/src/server/initServer');
const tasks = require('cypress-plugin-snapshots/src/tasks');

const initScreenshotPlugin = (on, globalConfig = {}) => {
  const config = initConfig(globalConfig.env[CONFIG_KEY]);
  initServer(config);

  globalConfig.env[CONFIG_KEY] = JSON.stringify(config);

  // Here I removed the "on('before:browser:launch..."

  on('task', tasks);
}

module.exports = {
  initScreenshotPlugin
};
```


Now you can use your custom function for initializing the plugin.
```js
const { initScreenshotPlugin } = require("my-plugin-workaround");

module.exports = (on, config) => {
  on("before:browser:launch", (browser = {}, launchOptions) => {
        // ... 
  });
  initScreenshotPlugin(on, config);
  return config;
};
```

