You have a race condition in your code. Remember that cypress commands *add things to a queue*, they don't execute immediately - even things like `cy.intercept`, which seems like it might be synchronous, require talking over a websocket to the cypress server running on your machine.

For me, your original case works sometimes, and changes behavior between browsers (mostly failing on Firefox, mostly passing on Chromium) - definitely a race condition in there, which is why you're getting different behavior between component and e2e testing.

This sort of thing is very easy to miss - I spent quite a while trying to figure out what was going wrong. ^^;

You can fix this by using `cy.then()`, waiting to initialize your component (and make the call) until after your intercept / alias are set up.

