@tbiethman @ZachJW34 The observations about the double scroll are valid, but I think leaving it as-is might be the best solution for now (at least, within this PR). I get into it a little bit in the comments for the ticket: https://cypress-io.atlassian.net/browse/UNIFY-1169

The longer term plan is to go to full page scroll on this page, which is a maybe a can of worms when we think about the virtualized list, but it would solve the double scroll. The next best option (imo) would be to avoid having dynamic content above the virtualized list at all and show this on the spec runner page. I haven't gotten feedback on that idea yet, but it wouldn't be a big change to made codewise. 

When we have the dynamic content, letting the double scroll happen at least gives the user the option of getting a reasonably-sized list to appear, without being confined to the bottom half of the screen as the "right" size. If we handle the dynamic content by monitoring the alert's size and adjusting the fixed height of the list, I think the usability is actually a little worse.

